From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hIRoic Linux PoC <noreply@localhost>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 15:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] spi: stm32-qspi: apply ES0290 memory-map workaround

STM32F74x/F75x erratum ES0290 section 2.4.3 requires software to clear
QUADSPI_AR and abort the previous indirect read before entering
memory-mapped mode.  Without that sequence, U-Boot intermittently shifts a
QSPI read by one stale byte, causing a warm reboot to fail with "zimage:
Bad magic!".

Apply the documented sequence before programming CCR for a memory-mapped
operation.  This permits aligned and repeatable kernel and DTB loads.

Signed-off-by: hIRoic Linux PoC <noreply@localhost>
---
 drivers/spi/stm32_qspi.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/stm32_qspi.c b/drivers/spi/stm32_qspi.c
--- a/drivers/spi/stm32_qspi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/stm32_qspi.c
@@ -319,6 +319,26 @@ static int stm32_qspi_exec_op(struct spi_slave *slave,
 		ccr |= (_stm32_qspi_get_mode(op->data.buswidth)
 			<< STM32_QSPI_CCR_DMODE_SHIFT);
 
+	/*
+	 * STM32F74x/F75x erratum ES0290 2.4.3: an indirect operation can
+	 * leave AR[1:0] set and corrupt the first subsequent memory-mapped
+	 * read.  Clear AR and abort the old transaction before entering
+	 * memory-mapped mode.
+	 */
+	if (mode == STM32_QSPI_CCR_MEM_MAP) {
+		writel(0, &priv->regs->ar);
+		setbits_le32(&priv->regs->cr, STM32_QSPI_CR_ABORT);
+		timeout = readl_poll_timeout(&priv->regs->cr, cr,
+					     !(cr & STM32_QSPI_CR_ABORT),
+					     STM32_ABT_TIMEOUT_US);
+		if (timeout)
+			return timeout;
+
+		ret = _stm32_qspi_wait_for_not_busy(priv);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	writel(ccr, &priv->regs->ccr);
 
 	if (op->addr.nbytes && mode != STM32_QSPI_CCR_MEM_MAP)
-- 
2.52.0
